---
<Base title={title} description={description} path="/guides/how-to-compare-two-texts-for-differences.html">
  <aside class="ad-rail" aria-label="Advertisement"><div class="ad-slot ad-slot-rail"></div></aside>
  <div class="wrap article">
    <p class="note"><a href="/guides.html">Guides</a> / Text comparison</p>
    <h1>How to Compare Two Texts for Differences</h1>
    <p class="lead">When two drafts of a document look almost the same, a line-by-line comparison shows exactly what changed. It is faster and more reliable than reading both versions side by side.</p>
    <div class="ad-slot" aria-label="Advertisement"></div>
<h2>What a diff shows</h2>
<p>A diff compares two texts line by line and marks each line as added, removed or unchanged. The method finds the longest run of matching lines, then treats everything else as a change. That is why a moved paragraph shows up as a removal and an addition.</p>
<h2>Steps to compare</h2>
<ol>
<li>Copy the older version into the Original box.</li>
<li>Copy the newer version into the New version box.</li>
<li>Press Compare. Lines starting with a plus sign were added, lines with a minus sign were removed, and lines with two spaces are unchanged.</li>
</ol>
<h2>Tips for better results</h2>
<ul>
<li>Remove formatting before you compare, because bullet symbols and smart quotes can make identical lines look different.</li>
<li>Compare one section at a time when the texts are very long.</li>
<li>Check the counts at the top. A large number of changes may mean the wrong versions were pasted.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Try it yourself</h2>
<p>The <a href="/tools/text-diff-checker.html">Text Diff Checker</a> runs in your browser. The text you paste is not saved or sent anywhere.</p>
